# IIQ Java Naming Conventions

## Files

| Type | Convention | Example |
|------|-----------|---------|
| Java class | PascalCase + `.java` | `MetadataValidationResource.java` |
| Test file | Mirrors source + `Tests` suffix | `MetadataValidationServiceTests.java` |

## Java elements

| Element | Convention | Example |
|---------|-----------|---------|
| Class | PascalCase | `MetadataValidationService` |
| Method | camelCase, verb-first | `validateMetadata()`, `getValidationRules()` |
| Variable | camelCase | `validationResult`, `ruleList` |
| Constant | UPPER_SNAKE_CASE | `MAX_RESULTS`, `DEFAULT_PAGE_SIZE` |
| Package | lowercase | `sailpoint.web.rest`, `sailpoint.service` |
| REST path | lowercase, plural nouns | `/rest/ui/metadataValidationDefinitions` |

## Message keys referenced from Java

Backend resources that throw validation/error messages reference keys from `iiqMessages.properties`. Key format and authoring rules live in `iiq-naming-angularjs.mdc` (the primary consumer of the properties file).

Short version: `ui_{feature}_{component}_{action}`. Never hardcode user-facing strings in Java — always reference a key.
